{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>That gathers up all the camps.</b> Talmud Yerushalmi: Because the tribe of Dan was numerous in population, it traveled last, and whoever had lost something — it would return it to him. There are those who say they walked with a sign-board, and derive it from ״כַּאֲשֶׁר יַחֲנוּ כֵּן יִסָּעוּ״; and there are those who say they walked like a beam, and derive it from ״מְאַסֵּף לְכָל הַמַּחֲנֹת״ (Talmud Yerushalmi, Eruvin 5)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:12.524156522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}